Hello everyone, I just started playing Nethack since... umm... last 
night.  I'm sort of late to this whole thing.  (Though, I have been 
playing Moria on and off since 1986... that sort of counts?  A little bit?)

Anyway, I have a question for everyone:  I notice in the Nethack 
Guidebook it says you can 'train' your pet by throwing it food.  This 
seems like a good idea to me.  So, as I was just playing, I noticed my 
pet was quite hungry.  (Or I assume she was, since she kept biting me.) 
  So, I think to myself, I'll throw her some food!  The only problem is 
the game won't let me throw food.  It only lets me throw weapons.  I 
don't think throwing darts (or long swords, for that matter) at my pet 
is a good idea.

So, my question is:  Can I actually throw food like the Guidebook says? 
  If so, how?

And also, on an unrelated note, I have learned I do not know more than 
the collective whole of the Nethack community.  Stuff I read advised 
that you do not ever attack Floating Eyes, for they paralyze you and 
then something will come along and eat you.  So, I encountered a 
Floating Eye (on the 4th dungeon level) and thought, "There's nothing 
around here to hurt me!  Die, Floating Eyeball!"  Sadly, it paralyzed me 
and along came a giant beetle and ate me.

Oops.  There goes my first Nethack character.  Maybe he'll come back as 
a ghost and I can hit him in the head with an axe for being stupid.


Anyway, Nethack is much better than Moria.  Now I wish I hadn't played 
Moria for 20 years.  (Or at least played both concurrently.)


